  "Using a global threshold T derived from the distribution of point-to-centroid distances based on 3 standard deviations (sigma = 1.4826 * MAD_e).",
  "Evaluating performance on 10 datasets (2 standard datasets: Iris and Ruspini, and 4 outlier-contaminated versions of each with 5%, 10%, 15%, and 20% gross errors) over 100 runs.",
  "Comparing mean squared error between classical k-means and k-means-sharp (k-means#), and measuring k-means#'s accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score for outlier detection."
 ],
 "main_findings": [
